From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] oleacc: the window object, the window's parts, the caret, the cursor and buttons

oleacc's standard objects were mostly stubs: the OBJID_WINDOW object
answered nearly everything with E_NOTIMPL, CreateStdAccessibleObject
refused the title bar, menus, scroll bars, size grip, caret and cursor
("unhandled object id", E_NOTIMPL), and buttons had no role or action. As
documented for MSAA's standard objects now:

- The window object: ROLE_SYSTEM_WINDOW, its text as its name, a state
  from its style (invisible, unavailable, focusable, focused, moveable,
  sizeable, offscreen), its rectangle, its parent (the parent's or the
  desktop's client object), and seven parts as children in Windows' order
  (system menu, title bar, menu bar, client, vertical and horizontal
  scroll bars, size grip), enumerated, navigated (first and last child,
  next and previous part, sibling windows) and hit-tested through
  WM_NCHITTEST; SELFLAG_TAKEFOCUS takes the focus.
- New (nonclient.c): the title bar (five buttons, INDEX_TITLEBAR_*, their
  states from GetTitleBarInfo, places, and Press: SC_MINIMIZE,
  SC_MAXIMIZE/SC_RESTORE, SC_CONTEXTHELP, SC_CLOSE), the menu bar (its
  items, names without the ampersand, Alt+ shortcuts, states, Open or
  Execute), the system menu, the scroll bars (INDEX_SCROLLBAR_* parts from
  GetScrollBarInfo, the position as a percentage for get/put_accValue, the
  arrows and pages pressed as WM_VSCROLL/WM_HSCROLL), the size grip, the
  caret (from GetGUIThreadInfo) and the cursor (with no window too).
  Unknown object ids give E_INVALIDARG.
- Client objects: a top-level window's name is all its text and it has no
  keyboard shortcut (as Windows 10 1607 and later); SELFLAG_TAKEFOCUS,
  accNavigate (first/last child window, the parts beside the client),
  help topic, selection and IEnumVARIANT::Clone answer; buttons get their
  role by style (push button, check box, radio button, group box), their
  pressed, checked, mixed and default states, and their default action
  (Press, Check, Uncheck) done by BM_CLICK.
- winuser.h gets the INDEX_TITLEBAR_* and INDEX_SCROLLBAR_* constants.

13 of Wine's oleacc todos pass.

Gate: test/oleaccstd-gate.sh (test/oleaccstd-probe.c). Mutants
SG_MUTANT_NO_PARTS, SG_MUTANT_NO_PART_ACTION (oleacc/nonclient.c),
SG_MUTANT_NO_BUTTON_ACTION (oleacc/client.c).
